From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@loudthinking.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-asus-zenbook-a16: Drop rising-edge
 lid wakeup action

With wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>, gpio-keys arms the lid
hall-sensor interrupt (TLMM GPIO 92, active low) for the rising edge only.
When the SoC enters and exits CX collapse with the lid already open, the
lid IRQ fires immediately and aborts s2idle (~0.6 s after suspend),
matching the same Glymur lid-switch issue fixed on the Microsoft Surface
Laptop 8.

Drop wakeup-event-action so the lid switch wakes on either edge: opening
the lid still wakes the laptop from closed-lid sleep, and suspending with
the lid open stays asleep in CXSD/AOSD/DDR until a real wakeup event.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts	2026-11-27 14:06:19.864857416 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts	2026-11-27 14:06:19.866305741 +0100
@@ -76,7 +76,6 @@
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
 			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
 			wakeup-source;
-			wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>;
 		};
 	};
 
